## Objective

Build a production-style Payment Gateway abstraction that demonstrates abstract contracts, multiple implementations, polymorphism, composition, dependency inversion, and testability.

## Step 1 — Define the Contract

```dart
abstract interface class PaymentGateway {
  Future<void> pay(double amount);
}
```

This defines what a payment gateway must provide without exposing how the payment is processed.

## Step 2 — Production Implementation

```dart
class RazorpayGateway implements PaymentGateway {
  @override
  Future<void> pay(double amount) async {
    print('Processing Razorpay payment: $amount');
  }
}
```

The concrete implementation satisfies the contract.

## Step 3 — Test Implementation

```dart
class FakePaymentGateway implements PaymentGateway {
  @override
  Future<void> pay(double amount) async {
    print('Processing fake payment: $amount');
  }
}
```

The fake implementation can be used without connecting to a real payment provider.

## Step 4 — High-Level Consumer

```dart
class CheckoutService {
  final PaymentGateway gateway;

  CheckoutService(this.gateway);

  Future<void> checkout(double amount) {
    return gateway.pay(amount);
  }
}
```

The service depends on the abstraction rather than Razorpay directly.

## Step 5 — Production Usage

```dart
void main() async {
  final checkout = CheckoutService(
    RazorpayGateway(),
  );

  await checkout.checkout(999);
}
```

## Step 6 — Test Usage

```dart
void main() async {
  final checkout = CheckoutService(
    FakePaymentGateway(),
  );

  await checkout.checkout(999);
}
```

The consumer remains unchanged while the implementation is replaced.

## Step 7 — Flutter Integration

A Flutter application can place the abstraction behind the state/application layer:

```text
UI
 ↓
CheckoutViewModel
 ↓
CheckoutService
 ↓
PaymentGateway
 ↓
RazorpayGateway
 ↓
External Payment System
```

The UI should not directly construct or control the payment provider.

## Step 8 — Extension Challenge

Add another implementation:

```text
PaymentGateway
├── RazorpayGateway
├── StripeGateway
└── FakePaymentGateway
```

The `CheckoutService` should not require a change merely because another implementation was added.

## Step 9 — Contract Challenge

Add a second focused contract:

```dart
abstract interface class RefundGateway {
  Future<void> refund(String transactionId);
}
```

Then decide whether a concrete payment service should implement both contracts.

The objective is to distinguish focused contracts from one large interface.
